{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019eUQRGcrYVvz69twSh9qSq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The on-disk SV-001 fix seeds `sourceSeq`/`startTurnSeq` from `inspect.overview` durable counts so a resume continues past prior keys. I need to assess whether this is correct and robust. The crux is: **what does PI's `message_end` actually carry?** If there's a real durable entry id, the connector should anchor idempotency on that (stable across re-delivery) rather than a position counter. Let me read the PI types, the LHC inspect/intake surfaces, and the new tests."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12087,"cache_read_input_tokens":112923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12087},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24167eda-1813-43e8-bfbc-fbb2eb03ffb4","uuid":"8dee6e9e-9968-4e51-b724-fb6094e5cef2","request_id":"req_011Cc2p53qhayTXcxXLUaE4E"}
