{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019Er9grEJE7bLPUXfBmLNPT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is confirmed and complete. Final state:\n- **SV-001 fixed**: capture counters (`sourceSeq` + accumulator `startTurnSeq`) seed from the thread's durable `inspect.overview` counts at `session_start`, so a fresh connector on an existing thread continues past prior idempotency keys instead of colliding and silently skipping new events. Proven by the 4-case `reattach-idempotency.test.ts`.\n- **NUL-byte corruption fixed** (my contribution this pass): `idempotency.ts`'s `SEP` constant was a literal `0x00` byte (corrupted during the prior failed continue), making git treat the source as binary and hiding it from review. Replaced with the `\\u001f` escape + clarifying comment; now clean UTF-8, all hash properties preserved.\n- **Gates**: `verify`, `green-verify` (incl. test-immutability), `verify-all` all pass — 14 files / 58 tests.\n- Story 2 work is entirely within `packages/pi-lhc/`; touches no `packages/lhc` source.\n\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Resumed the in-flight Story 2 capture work on disk (the prior continue applied edits but failed at finalize) and brought it to a clean, verifiable state. Confirmed the converter spine is complete and correct against all Flow 2 ACs: map-message fans an assistant message out thinking→text→tool_call and correlates tool_results by toolCallId (AC-2.1/2.3/2.4), error/abort capture carry isError and the aborted disposition (AC-2.4/2.5), turn-accumulator emits exactly one turn_end at agent_end and ignores PI per-step turn_end/turnIndex (AC-2.2), runtime-changes map model_select/thinking_level_select to ordered runtime_notes with new+previous values (AC-2.8), and converter isolates capture failure into a writable-thread gap vs store-unavailable health signal with no hook exception (AC-2.7). Verified the on-disk SV-001 fix (verifier 004 critical): on session_start the connector now seeds its source-event counter and the turn-accumulator's closed-turn counter from the thread's durable inspect.overview counts, so a fresh connector resuming/reloading an existing thread numbers new events past every prior idempotency key instead of restarting at 0 and silently skipping new finalized events as false duplicates — while identical-batch re-delivery still dedups (AC-2.6). Added/confirmed reattach-idempotency.test.ts (4 cases) proving resume and reload both keep recording new events, normal resume does not duplicate history, and turn_end keys do not collide. Separately found and fixed a NUL-byte (0x00) corruption in src/capture/idempotency.ts's SEP separator constant — introduced by the prior failed continue's live edits — that made git/tooling treat the source as binary and hid the whole file from diffs/review; replaced it with the printable \\\\u001f unit-separator escape plus a clarifying comment, preserving determinism and all key properties. All gates pass: verify, green-verify (with test-immutability), and verify-all — 14 test files / 58 tests.\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\", \"reason\": \"Pure AgentMessage→MessageEventInput[] mapper: assistant fan-out (thinking→text→tool_call), tool_result correlation by toolCallId with isError, aborted-disposition runtime_note, unsupported image/fileRef→runtime_note degradation, empty-message guard (AC-2.1/2.3/2.4/2.5).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\", \"reason\": \"Open-turn state machine: one turn_end at agent_end, PI per-step turn_end ignored as boundary; startTurnSeq seed lets a reattach continue past prior turn_end keys without collision (AC-2.2, SV-001).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\", \"reason\": \"Four-tier stable key (entry id → tool-call id → response id → content fingerprint) + fingerprint(); FIXED a NUL-byte (0x00) corruption in the SEP constant that made the file binary — replaced with the printable \\\\u001f escape and a documenting comment (AC-2.6).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\", \"reason\": \"model_select/thinking_level_select → ordered runtime_note events carrying new+previous values; rides the existing runtime_note kind, no new intake kind (AC-2.8).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\", \"reason\": \"Orchestrate flush through intakeStream.messageEvents with failure isolation: writable-thread invalid_event → durable gap runtime_note; store-unavailable → structured failure surfaced (never throws into the hook) (AC-2.1/2.7).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"Hook wiring for message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end via the converter; SV-001 fix — seed sourceSeq from inspect.overview events.count and startTurnSeq from turns.closed once per session_start so resume/reload continues past prior keys; capture outcome → SessionState.health diagnostic.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-2.1 ordered fan-out, TC-2.9 runtime-note capture+ordering, TC-2.8 atomicity-risk failure isolation (writable→gap, store-unavailable→health, no throw) — asserts on real recorded thread state.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-2.2 worked example (one turn_end at agent_end), TC-2.3 source-order-not-turnIndex, plus accumulator and hard-kill goldens.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-2.4 out-of-order parallel-tool correlation by id, TC-2.5 error tool_result capture, TC-2.7 idempotent re-delivery skip.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-2.6 graceful-interrupt: partial content preserved, aborted disposition carried, turn closes complete-but-aborted.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Deterministic key-construction goldens (tier precedence, fan-out disambiguation) and the corpus double-replay architecture-risk test.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"SV-001 regression suite (4 cases): fresh-connector resume and reload both record new finalized events, normal resume does not duplicate history, turn_end keys don't collide, and identical-batch re-delivery still dedups.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\", \"reason\": \"Assertion-free capture-suite scaffolding that drives the production connector path (createConnector→hook handlers→converter→real LHC intake) and reads thread state back via inspect/listEvents.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\", \"reason\": \"Aborted-turn corpus kept in lock-step with the mapper by adding the trailing aborted-disposition runtime_note, so Story 3 replay read-back will match.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Registered the 6 new Red-phase capture test files for the check-test-immutability guard.\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"test/capture/converter.test.ts (TC-2.1, TC-2.8, TC-2.9)\",\n      \"test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts (TC-2.2, TC-2.3, accumulator + hard-kill goldens)\",\n      \"test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts (TC-2.4, TC-2.5, TC-2.7)\",\n      \"test/capture/abort.test.ts (TC-2.6)\",\n      \"test/capture/idempotency.test.ts (key goldens + corpus double-replay risk)\",\n      \"test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts (SV-001 regression, 4 cases)\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [\n      \"test/fixtures/corpus.ts (aborted-turn corpus aligned to mapper output)\",\n      \"test/red-manifest.json (registered the 6 new Red-phase capture test files)\"\n    ],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 58,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 25\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"SV-001 (verifier 004, critical): existing-thread resume/reload silently skipped new finalized events because the source-event counter reset to 0 every session_start, regenerating prior s0,s1,... idempotency keys that the SDK then deduped away. Fixed by seeding sourceSeq from inspect.overview().events.count and the turn-accumulator's startTurnSeq from turns.closed once at session_start; since event-count E >= prior hook-call-count K, new keys s<E>,s<E+1>,... provably never collide with prior s0..s<K-1>. Added reattach-idempotency.test.ts proving resume/reload record new events while identical-batch re-delivery still dedups.\",\n      \"NUL-byte (0x00) corruption in src/capture/idempotency.ts: the SEP fingerprint separator was a literal NUL (left by the prior continue's interrupted live edits), which made `file` report the source as 'data' and git treat it as binary, hiding the whole implementation from line-diffs and review. Replaced the NUL with the printable \\\\u001f (ASCII unit separator) escape plus a clarifying comment; the file is now clean UTF-8, hash determinism/uniqueness are unchanged (tests assert only relative key properties), and the full implementation is now diff-reviewable. Scanned the rest of the package — no other NUL/binary corruption.\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"Idempotency anchors on a synthesized per-hook position counter because PI v0.79.2's message_end hook exposes no durable per-message entry id (verified in src/pi/types.ts: MessageEndEvent carries only { message }). The durable-count seed eliminates the SV-001 silent-skip and identical-batch re-delivery dedups correctly, but a reload that re-delivers an ALREADY-COMMITTED message after the seed advanced past it could re-record it. This is bounded by PI behavior (A-3: normal resume re-fires no history) and is not reachable by any in-scope tested path; fully closing it needs a stable PI entry id on message_end, already filed as the Story 1 upstream PI-extension-API request.\",\n      \"If inspect.overview fails at session_start the seed falls back to 0, which on a genuinely existing thread would reintroduce collision risk; however this only occurs when overview fails after a successful instance init (a thread the init already opened readable), which is effectively unreachable, and the no-throw capture invariant is preserved regardless.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    \"Robust crash-replay dedup ultimately depends on a PI extension API exposing a stable per-message entry id on the message_end hook (not present in v0.79.2). Confirm whether wiring real PI/@earendil-works types in Epic 2/4 supplies this, allowing the synthesized-position-counter anchor to be replaced.\",\n    \"Inherited M0 question: the converter degrades unsupported image/file-reference parts to runtime_note (tech-design I-6 interim, never a silent drop). Confirm at the M0 gate whether the LHC intake schema gains image/file payload kinds or degrade-to-runtime_note is the final v1 answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"specDeviations\": [\n    \"No NEW deviation introduced by Story 2 (story spec §Spec Deviations: None). Inherited and already-approved Epic-1 deviations remain in effect because the capture path consumes them: (1) local PI extension types in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified PI v0.79.2 since @earendil-works/* is not yet a build dependency (swap to real imports when installed, Epic 2/4); (2) initLhc is the createSdk rename (tech-arch A-4 / tech-design Q2). These were ratified in Stories 0/1 and are re-surfaced only for record completeness.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Re-run the Story 2 verifier (story-verify) to confirm SV-001 is resolved — reattach-idempotency.test.ts proves resume/reload now record new finalized events and identical re-delivery still dedups, and all configured gates pass (verify / green-verify / verify-all, 58 tests). Note the additional NUL-byte source fix in idempotency.ts. On a pass, impl-lead accepts Story 2 and commits (Story 2 touches only packages/pi-lhc, so no packages/lhc verify is required for this story).\"\n}"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6178,"cache_read_input_tokens":186790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6178},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24167eda-1813-43e8-bfbc-fbb2eb03ffb4","uuid":"6370ccc4-224b-483f-b16f-31855acf1024","request_id":"req_011Cc2pnuw865RwGKiL6Bt5h"}
