 [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 58,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 25\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"SV-001 (verifier 004, critical): existing-thread resume/reload silently skipped new finalized events because the source-event counter reset to 0 every session_start, regenerating prior s0,s1,... idempotency keys that the SDK then deduped away. Fixed by seeding sourceSeq from inspect.overview().events.count and the turn-accumulator's startTurnSeq from turns.closed once at session_start; since event-count E >= prior hook-call-count K, new keys s<E>,s<E+1>,... provably never collide with prior s0..s<K-1>. Added reattach-idempotency.test.ts proving resume/reload record new events while identical-batch re-delivery still dedups.\",\n      \"NUL-byte (0x00) corruption in src/capture/idempotency.ts: the SEP fingerprint separator was a literal NUL (left by the prior continue's interrupted live edits), which made `file` report the source as 'data' and git treat it as binary, hiding the whole implementation from line-diffs and review. Replaced the NUL with the printable \\\\u001f (ASCII unit separator) escape plus a clarifying comment; the file is now clean UTF-8, hash determinism/uniqueness are unchanged (tests assert only relative key properties), and the full implementation is now diff-reviewable. Scanned the rest of the package — no other NUL/binary corruption.\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"Idempotency anchors on a synthesized per-hook position counter because PI v0.79.2's message_end hook exposes no durable per-message entry id (verified in src/pi/types.ts: MessageEndEvent carries only { message }). The durable-count seed eliminates the SV-001 silent-skip and identical-batch re-delivery dedups correctly, but a reload that re-delivers an ALREADY-COMMITTED message after the seed advanced past it could re-record it. This is bounded by PI behavior (A-3: normal resume re-fires no history) and is not reachable by any in-scope tested path; fully closing it needs a stable PI entry id on message_end, already filed as the Story 1 upstream PI-extension-API request.\",\n      \"If inspect.overview fails at session_start the seed falls back to 0, which on a genuinely existing thread would reintroduce collision risk; however this only occurs when overview fails after a successful instance init (a thread the init already opened readable), which is effectively unreachable, and the no-throw capture invariant is preserved regardless.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    \"Robust crash-replay dedup ultimately depends on a PI extension API exposing a stable per-message entry id on the message_end hook (not present in v0.79.2). Confirm whether wiring real PI/@earendil-works types in Epic 2/4 supplies this, allowing the synthesized-position-counter anchor to be replaced.\",\n    \"Inherited M0 question: the converter degrades unsupported image/file-reference parts to runtime_note (tech-design I-6 interim, never a silent drop). Confirm at the M0 gate whether the LHC intake schema gains image/file payload kinds or degrade-to-runtime_note is the final v1 answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"specDeviations\": [\n    \"No NEW deviation introduced by Story 2 (story spec §Spec Deviations: None). Inherited and already-approved Epic-1 deviations remain in effect because the capture path consumes them: (1) local PI extension types in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified PI v0.79.2 since @earendil-works/* is not yet a build dependency (swap to real imports when installed, Epic 2/4); (2) initLhc is the createSdk rename (tech-arch A-4 / tech-design Q2). These were ratified in Stories 0/1 and are re-surfaced only for record completeness.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Re-run the Story 2 verifier (story-verify) to confirm SV-001 is resolved — reattach-idempotency.test.ts proves resume/reload now record new finalized events and identical re-delivery still dedups, and all configured gates pass (verify / green-verify / verify-all, 58 tests). Note the additional NUL-byte source fix in idempotency.ts. On a pass, impl-lead accepts Story 2 and commits (Story 2 touches only packages/pi-lhc, so no packages/lhc verify is required for this story).\"\n}","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"24167eda-1813-43e8-bfbc-fbb2eb03ffb4","total_cost_usd":4.9706075,"usage":{"input_tokens":4257,"cache_creation_input_tokens":177611,"cache_read_input_tokens":3646549,"output_tokens":53930,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":177611,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6634,"cache_read_input_tokens":186790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6178,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6178},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1608,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001688,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":4257,"outputTokens":53930,"cacheReadInputTokens":3646549,"cacheCreationInputTokens":177611,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.9689195,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9ddcf09c-8551-4554-a256-0977336c87df"}
